{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/3270","id":5267176885,"node_id":"PR_kwDODboMws8AAAABOfK9tQ","html_url":"https://github.com/teststuffstash/homelab/pull/3270","diff_url":"https://github.com/teststuffstash/homelab/pull/3270.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/teststuffstash/homelab/pull/3270.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/issues/3270","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/3270/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/3270/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/issues/3270/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/statuses/2c9b66f3a1925d96de3a8823e93e04d83443d752","number":3270,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Goal #3118 assembly: the gateway reads the Go account headroom","user":{"login":"homelab-agents-1234[bot]","id":297114375,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOEbWbBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97731433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/homelab-agents-1234","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/homelab-agents-1234%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\nAssembly of Goal #3118 — the gateway reads the Go account headroom. Both children merged into `goal/3118-go-headroom`: #3108 (PR #3260, GW-SESSIONS-ADMIT Go headroom poll) and #3119 (PR #3125, GW-SESSIONS-OUTCOME relayed-429 no-strike).\n\nCoverage map:\n- Acceptance 1 (ADMIT Go headroom rows; gap flags/rows removed; Go draw demoted to a lower bound): #3108 / PR #3260.\n- Acceptance 2 (OUTCOME \"consumer outcome after a relayed 429 strikes nothing\" + boundary rows): #3119 / PR #3125.\n- Acceptance 3 (deployed `policy.json` `rails.opencode.headroom`, ceiling 0.80): post-launch, after the image carrying acceptance 1 is deployed — deferred to the Goal's post-launch leg.\n- Acceptance 4 (production accepted-report + first `quota-limited` defer): production evidence, post-launch.\n- Open/deferred: #3269 (judge-path outcome row, deferred by the checkpoint, from PR #3125 review); post-launch bucket #3127.\n\nSpec changes:\n\n- GW-SESSIONS-CAPACITY §Go account headroom gains 13 cases (11 admission rows + 2 poll rows): fresh admission; ceiling exhaustion ⚖; later reset across exhausted windows ⚖; non-ok status limits ⚖; \"no reading yet is unknown — fail closed ⚖\"; \"a stale reading is stale ⚖\"; whole-report refusal for missing windows and passed resets; continuing the walk; compatibility without a headroom block ⚖; unset URL sends no poll and fails closed ⚖; and, in the poll table, Go-key authorization and no identity in logs.\n- ⚖ the Go rail fails closed on no reading and on a stale reading (`quota-unknown` / `quota-stale` defer), where the anthropic window reading on the same page fails open (\"an unavailable reading admits, never blocks\"). Reason: the reading exists so that no ride is admitted onto an exhausted Go block and meets the 429 there; the Go allowance is one account pool under every Go model, and the worker's walk has a next rail to continue on. The cost is accepted: if the vendor's usage endpoint stops answering, the Go rail stops admitting until a reading is accepted again.\n- §Go account headroom now states the retry: `retry_after_s` is the latest reset among the windows at or above the ceiling, else the policy's `defer_retry_s` (60 s) — for a non-`ok` status under the ceiling, `quota-unknown` and `quota-stale` — as GW-CODEX-ADMISSION rules for the codex rail (replaces \"the default hold\").\n- GW-SESSIONS-CAPACITY preamble: the sentence saying every reading arrives through the data plane is removed (the Go account reading arrives by the gateway's own poll).\n- Add policy-go world and its byte-identical test twin: max_age_s 120, ceiling 0.95, named rolling/weekly/monthly windows and poll_interval_s 30 are fixture choices ⚖, not production policy. Document the world in worlds/README.md.\n- Remove the Go headroom gap flag from the sessions coupling table and specs index. Remove the two former Go gap rows: their unimplemented claims are replaced by the account poll/admission rows; no green proof is removed.\n- Describe Go window draw as a lower bound of the shared account pool, retained as a belt beneath the reading ⚖. The existing draw rows remain.\n- Shared headroom normalization keys windows by policy profile entry; Codex retains its minute profile. Its existing upstream-header assertion changes only from w.minutes to w.key, preserving the same proof.\n- GW-SESSIONS-OUTCOME gains a table \"After a relayed 429\" with three rows: \"a consumer outcome after a relayed 429 strikes nothing ⚖\" (`upstream-429` then consumer `unknown`: no counted strike, outcome stored); \"a harness that gave up on a 429 strikes nothing ⚖\"; \"a 429 followed by a 2xx is no capacity death ⚖\" (one model-scoped `unknown` strike). §Refutation gains one row: \"a clean outcome after a 429 still refutes ⚖\" (its `sequence` cell now names the model, `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`).\n\nAssembly-for: #3118\n<!-- agent-touches: begin -->\nTouches: undeclared\n<!-- agent-touches: end -->\n\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-11T21:42:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T17:51:58Z","closed_at":"2026-11-12T17:51:56Z","merged_at":"2026-11-12T17:51:56Z","merge_commit_sha":"0d2f4926c56b330711b9ee1b8532b988538cab6c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"teststuffstash:goal/3118-go-headroom","ref":"goal/3118-go-headroom","repo":{"id":230296770,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkyMzAyOTY3NzA=","name":"homelab","full_name":"teststuffstash/homelab","owner":{"login":"teststuffstash","id":97731433,"node_id":"O_kgDOBdNDaQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97731433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash","html_url":"https://github.com/teststuffstash","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teststuffstash/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Agentic software delivery on its own Talos Kubernetes platform — research shapes goals, agents ride issues to CI-verified PRs, and production closes each goal validated or reverted. Boot-from-git, no click-ops.","homepage